# MiniMax M3 — 427.0B total / ~23B active MoE, 1M context (we cap at 262144).
#
# BLOCKED: nothing in this repo's H100 lineup can load the checkpoint named below.
# Hugging Face API, queried 2026-09-09Z, MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3 safetensors.parameters:
#
#   {BF16: 426,993,800,960, F32: 46,339,200}   = 427,040,140,160 params
#   BF16 weights (2 bytes/param, + F32 at 4)   = ~854 GB
#   4x H100 SXM5 = 320 GB, 8x H100 SXM5 = 640 GB
#
# So ~854 GB does not fit 4x, and does not fit 8x either — before a single KV-cache block.
#
# The "~230 GB FP8 weight size" this file used to assert is wrong under every reading, and
# it is what put TP=4 here: MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3-FP8 is not pullable (the HF API answers an
# anonymous query with HTTP 401 — absent or private), and the official
# MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3-MXFP8 is ~444 GB (F8_E4M3 423,670,579,200 + U8 13,239,705,600 at
# 1 byte, BF16 3,323,221,760 at 2, F32 46,339,200 at 4) — which needs 8x H100, not 4x.
#
# What is open is therefore a CHECKPOINT decision, not a TP knob:
#   a. MXFP8 on 8x H100 — but every other model in the lineup runs its NATIVE precision, so
#      quantising this one is the same study-design confound as AI-3158 (qwen3-coder-next).
#   b. B200, where BF16 might fit — needs a live capacity/price check (no LAMBDA_API_KEY
#      here), and 8x B200 is the most expensive line in the RUNBOOK §5 budget.
# Nobody has loaded either. Do not dispatch this model until (a) or (b) is decided.
#
# TP/INSTANCE_TYPE below are the smallest H100 configuration that could ever hold this
# model under (a) — deliberately not the 4x that silently could not. They are a
# not-too-small placeholder, NOT a validated launch config.
HF_REPO="MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-M3"
TP=8
MAX_MODEL_LEN=262144
# vLLM refuses tool_choice:"auto" without BOTH of these, and the harness agent loop
# sends exactly that on every call, so an attempt cannot start without them (AI-3159).
# The parser is per-model-family, which is why it lives here and not in the held
# constants. minimax_m3 is an exact-version parser in vLLM 0.28.0 and matches the
# <tool_call>/<tools> markers in this repo's chat template.
EXTRA_ARGS="--trust-remote-code --enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser minimax_m3"
INSTANCE_TYPE="gpu_8x_h100_sxm5"
